{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5932",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unmaintained, unsafe by design, and has known security issues"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GO-2026-5932\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: \nLink: [GO-2026-5932]()\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GO-2026-5932**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/crypto||[GO-2026-5932]()|\n\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-68121",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "crypto/tls: crypto/tls: Incorrect certificate validation during TLS session resumption"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During session resumption in crypto/tls, if the underlying Config has its ClientCAs or RootCAs fields mutated between the initial handshake and the resumed handshake, the resumed handshake may succeed when it should have failed. This may happen when a user calls Config.Clone and mutates the returned Config, or uses Config.GetConfigForClient. This can cause a client to resume a session with a server that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake, or cause a server to resume a session with a client that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68121",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-68121\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.24.13, 1.25.7, 1.26.0-rc.3\nLink: [CVE-2025-68121](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68121)\nDuring session resumption in crypto/tls, if the underlying Config has its ClientCAs or RootCAs fields mutated between the initial handshake and the resumed handshake, the resumed handshake may succeed when it should have failed. This may happen when a user calls Config.Clone and mutates the returned Config, or uses Config.GetConfigForClient. This can cause a client to resume a session with a server that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake, or cause a server to resume a session with a client that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-68121**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|stdlib|1.24.13, 1.25.7, 1.26.0-rc.3|[CVE-2025-68121](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68121)|\n\nDuring session resumption in crypto/tls, if the underlying Config has its ClientCAs or RootCAs fields mutated between the initial handshake and the resumed handshake, the resumed handshake may succeed when it should have failed. This may happen when a user calls Config.Clone and mutates the returned Config, or uses Config.GetConfigForClient. This can cause a client to resume a session with a server that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake, or cause a server to resume a session with a client that it would not have resumed with during the initial handshake."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 10,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "10.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61726",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang: net/url: Memory exhaustion in query parameter parsing in net/url"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/url package does not set a limit on the number of query parameters in a query. While the maximum size of query parameters in URLs is generally limited by the maximum request header size, the net/http.Request.ParseForm method can parse large URL-encoded forms. Parsing a large form containing many unique query parameters can cause excessive memory consumption."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61726",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-61726\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.24.12, 1.25.6\nLink: [CVE-2025-61726](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61726)\nThe net/url package does not set a limit on the number of query parameters in a query. While the maximum size of query parameters in URLs is generally limited by the maximum request header size, the net/http.Request.ParseForm method can parse large URL-encoded forms. Parsing a large form containing many unique query parameters can cause excessive memory consumption.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-61726**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.24.12, 1.25.6|[CVE-2025-61726](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61726)|\n\nThe net/url package does not set a limit on the number of query parameters in a query. While the maximum size of query parameters in URLs is generally limited by the maximum request header size, the net/http.Request.ParseForm method can parse large URL-encoded forms. Parsing a large form containing many unique query parameters can cause excessive memory consumption."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61729",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "crypto/x509: golang: Denial of Service due to excessive resource consumption via crafted certificate"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Within HostnameError.Error(), when constructing an error string, there is no limit to the number of hosts that will be printed out. Furthermore, the error string is constructed by repeated string concatenation, leading to quadratic runtime. Therefore, a certificate provided by a malicious actor can result in excessive resource consumption."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61729",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-61729\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.24.11, 1.25.5\nLink: [CVE-2025-61729](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61729)\nWithin HostnameError.Error(), when constructing an error string, there is no limit to the number of hosts that will be printed out. Furthermore, the error string is constructed by repeated string concatenation, leading to quadratic runtime. Therefore, a certificate provided by a malicious actor can result in excessive resource consumption.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-61729**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.24.11, 1.25.5|[CVE-2025-61729](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61729)|\n\nWithin HostnameError.Error(), when constructing an error string, there is no limit to the number of hosts that will be printed out. Furthermore, the error string is constructed by repeated string concatenation, leading to quadratic runtime. Therefore, a certificate provided by a malicious actor can result in excessive resource consumption."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25679",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "net/url: Incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals in net/url"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "url.Parse insufficiently validated the host/authority component and accepted some invalid URLs."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25679",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-25679\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.8, 1.26.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-25679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25679)\nurl.Parse insufficiently validated the host/authority component and accepted some invalid URLs.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-25679**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.25.8, 1.26.1|[CVE-2026-25679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-25679)|\n\nurl.Parse insufficiently validated the host/authority component and accepted some invalid URLs."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27145",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "crypto/x509: golang: golang crypto/x509: Denial of Service via excessive processing of DNS SAN entries"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(*x509.Certificate).VerifyHostname previously called matchHostnames in a loop over all DNS Subject Alternative Name (SAN) entries. This caused strings.Split(host, \".\") to execute repeatedly on the same input hostname. With a large DNS SAN list, verification costs scaled quadratically based on the number of SAN entries multiplied by the hostname's label count. Because x509.Verify validates hostnames before building the certificate chain, this overhead occurred even for untrusted certificates."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27145",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-27145\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.11, 1.26.4\nLink: [CVE-2026-27145](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27145)\n(*x509.Certificate).VerifyHostname previously called matchHostnames in a loop over all DNS Subject Alternative Name (SAN) entries. This caused strings.Split(host, \".\") to execute repeatedly on the same input hostname. With a large DNS SAN list, verification costs scaled quadratically based on the number of SAN entries multiplied by the hostname's label count. Because x509.Verify validates hostnames before building the certificate chain, this overhead occurred even for untrusted certificates.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-27145**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.25.11, 1.26.4|[CVE-2026-27145](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27145)|\n\n(*x509.Certificate).VerifyHostname previously called matchHostnames in a loop over all DNS Subject Alternative Name (SAN) entries. This caused strings.Split(host, \".\") to execute repeatedly on the same input hostname. With a large DNS SAN list, verification costs scaled quadratically based on the number of SAN entries multiplied by the hostname's label count. Because x509.Verify validates hostnames before building the certificate chain, this overhead occurred even for untrusted certificates."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32280",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "crypto/x509: crypto/tls: golang: Go: Denial of Service vulnerability in certificate chain building"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During chain building, the amount of work that is done is not correctly limited when a large number of intermediate certificates are passed in VerifyOptions.Intermediates, which can lead to a denial of service. This affects both direct users of crypto/x509 and users of crypto/tls."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32280",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-32280\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.9, 1.26.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-32280](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32280)\nDuring chain building, the amount of work that is done is not correctly limited when a large number of intermediate certificates are passed in VerifyOptions.Intermediates, which can lead to a denial of service. This affects both direct users of crypto/x509 and users of crypto/tls.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-32280**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.25.9, 1.26.2|[CVE-2026-32280](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32280)|\n\nDuring chain building, the amount of work that is done is not correctly limited when a large number of intermediate certificates are passed in VerifyOptions.Intermediates, which can lead to a denial of service. This affects both direct users of crypto/x509 and users of crypto/tls."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32281",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "crypto/x509: golang: Go crypto/x509: Denial of Service via inefficient certificate chain validation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Validating certificate chains which use policies is unexpectedly inefficient when certificates in the chain contain a very large number of policy mappings, possibly causing denial of service. This only affects validation of otherwise trusted certificate chains, issued by a root CA in the VerifyOptions.Roots CertPool, or in the system certificate pool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32281",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-32281\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.9, 1.26.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-32281](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32281)\nValidating certificate chains which use policies is unexpectedly inefficient when certificates in the chain contain a very large number of policy mappings, possibly causing denial of service. This only affects validation of otherwise trusted certificate chains, issued by a root CA in the VerifyOptions.Roots CertPool, or in the system certificate pool.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-32281**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.25.9, 1.26.2|[CVE-2026-32281](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32281)|\n\nValidating certificate chains which use policies is unexpectedly inefficient when certificates in the chain contain a very large number of policy mappings, possibly causing denial of service. This only affects validation of otherwise trusted certificate chains, issued by a root CA in the VerifyOptions.Roots CertPool, or in the system certificate pool."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32283",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "crypto/tls: golang: Go crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple TLS 1.3 key update messages"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If one side of the TLS connection sends multiple key update messages post-handshake in a single record, the connection can deadlock, causing uncontrolled consumption of resources. This can lead to a denial of service. This only affects TLS 1.3."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32283",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-32283\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.9, 1.26.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-32283](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32283)\nIf one side of the TLS connection sends multiple key update messages post-handshake in a single record, the connection can deadlock, causing uncontrolled consumption of resources. This can lead to a denial of service. This only affects TLS 1.3.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-32283**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|stdlib|1.25.9, 1.26.2|[CVE-2026-32283](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32283)|\n\nIf one side of the TLS connection sends multiple key update messages post-handshake in a single record, the connection can deadlock, causing uncontrolled consumption of resources. This can lead to a denial of service. This only affects TLS 1.3."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
