            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-47910",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "net/http: CrossOriginProtection bypass in net/http"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When using http.CrossOriginProtection, the AddInsecureBypassPattern method can unexpectedly bypass more requests than intended. CrossOriginProtection then skips validation, but forwards the original request path, which may be served by a different handler without the intended security protections."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47910",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-47910\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.1\nLink: [CVE-2025-47910](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47910)\nWhen using http.CrossOriginProtection, the AddInsecureBypassPattern method can unexpectedly bypass more requests than intended. CrossOriginProtection then skips validation, but forwards the original request path, which may be served by a different handler without the intended security protections.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-47910**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|stdlib|1.25.1|[CVE-2025-47910](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47910)|\n\nWhen using http.CrossOriginProtection, the AddInsecureBypassPattern method can unexpectedly bypass more requests than intended. CrossOriginProtection then skips validation, but forwards the original request path, which may be served by a different handler without the intended security protections."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-47912",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "net/url: Insufficient validation of bracketed IPv6 hostnames in net/url"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Parse function permits values other than IPv6 addresses to be included in square brackets within the host component of a URL. RFC 3986 permits IPv6 addresses to be included within the host component, enclosed within square brackets. For example: \"http://[::1]/\". IPv4 addresses and hostnames must not appear within square brackets. Parse did not enforce this requirement."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47912",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-47912\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.24.8, 1.25.2\nLink: [CVE-2025-47912](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47912)\nThe Parse function permits values other than IPv6 addresses to be included in square brackets within the host component of a URL. RFC 3986 permits IPv6 addresses to be included within the host component, enclosed within square brackets. For example: \"http://[::1]/\". IPv4 addresses and hostnames must not appear within square brackets. Parse did not enforce this requirement.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-47912**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|stdlib|1.24.8, 1.25.2|[CVE-2025-47912](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47912)|\n\nThe Parse function permits values other than IPv6 addresses to be included in square brackets within the host component of a URL. RFC 3986 permits IPv6 addresses to be included within the host component, enclosed within square brackets. For example: \"http://[::1]/\". IPv4 addresses and hostnames must not appear within square brackets. Parse did not enforce this requirement."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58183",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang: archive/tar: Unbounded allocation when parsing GNU sparse map"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58183",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-58183\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.24.8, 1.25.2\nLink: [CVE-2025-58183](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58183)\ntar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-58183**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|stdlib|1.24.8, 1.25.2|[CVE-2025-58183](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58183)|\n\ntar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
